 "old_string": "Check each panel's marker count independently and verify output dimensions equal the number of panel bands by panel columns. Preserve no separator rows/columns in the output.",
 "new_string": "Check each panel's marker count independently and verify output dimensions equal the number of panel bands by panel columns. Preserve no separator rows/columns in the output.\n\n### Rectangular panel layout variant: 8x19 test\nSeparators are full color-2 rows 2 and 5 and full color-2 columns 3, 7, 11, 15 (zero-based); these create 3 row bands × 5 column panels. Background is 7 and sparse marker is 3. Use the same threshold: panel has at least two markers → output 1; zero or one marker → output 7. Correct output for the accepted test was `[[7,7,7,7,1],[7,1,7,7,7],[7,7,1,7,7]]`.\n\nImportant distinction: do not assume every panel dimension is uniform or infer separators by color alone without checking full lines. In this test, the rightmost panel of the top band had two markers, the second panel of the middle band had two, and the center panel of the bottom band had two; several panels had exactly one marker and must remain 7. The previous incorrect submission missed the bottom-band center panel, so count all panel markers systematically, including every row/column in each cell of the partition."
}
